{
  "dom_id": "step-q345609",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "An economist measured $4$ particular features, ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3},{x}_{4},$ for each currency in a collection under devaluation. The collected data was stored in the standardized observation matrix $X,$ where each row contains measurements for a particular currency.\nThe singular values of $X$ are \n\n$$\n{\\sigma }_{1}=12,\\,{\\sigma }_{2}=7,\\,{\\sigma }_{3}=3,\\,{\\sigma }_{4}=1.\n$$\n\nThe economist then converted the original observation matrix $X$ into a new matrix $Y$ using the equation $Y=X{V}_{1},$ where ${V}_{1}$ is the $4\\times 1$ matrix consisting of the first principal component of the data. What percentage of the original variance is preserved in the new transformed matrix $Y$ compared to the initial observation matrix $X?$",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
